Z||000010||Bill Osmer||11-01-1999||12:35 PM||||After having repaired/replaced the cruise control wiring on my 86 GT, I also agree - it's the cruise control connector. There are four wires going to this connector - two on one side and two on the other. This is an inexpensive connector technique - it's made of the same material that printed circuits are, with metalized traces. It mates to a plastic connector that will be found up beside the steering column (assuming that this vehicle has cruise control, and hasn't had a steering wheel/column transplant)||||reg||1
